{
  "comment": "The theme catalogue, shared by the Flutter app and the native Apple app. Each theme names the identifying colours of its light and dark variant; the rest of the palette (container tints, legible separator and secondary label) is derived in code and pinned by shared/golden/themes/derived.json. After editing, run `python3 tools/generate_themes.py` to regenerate lib/src/theme/themes.g.dart and apple/CouncilCore/Sources/CouncilCore/Themes/ThemeCatalogue.g.swift, then `flutter test test/theme_golden_test.dart --dart-define=UPDATE_GOLDENS=true`. Order is the picker's order; \"default\" is reserved for the platform look and is not listed. Colours are #RRGGBB, or #AARRGGBB with alpha. Fields: bg = page behind grouped content; surface = a cell on the page; surface2 = a control on a cell; text; subtext = secondary text; separator; accent; onAccent = text on the accent; error (optional, else the derivation's default).",
